{# Go cross-package POJO struct template — emits openrtb_ext/imp_{bidder}.go

The struct lives in the shared `openrtb_ext` package (NOT under
`adapters/{bidder}/`), per upstream convention. Every adapter that
parses imp.ext.bidder.{bidder} fields needs a corresponding ExtImp{X}
struct here.

Inputs:
  ctx.bidder_class_root  : str  — PascalCase struct root (e.g., "Kobler", "AdkernelAdn")
  ctx.fields             : list[dict]  — per-field; each:
      go_name        : str  — Go field name (PascalCase, exported)
      json_tag       : str  — JSON wire-format property name
      go_type        : str  — Go type ("string", "int", "*int", "bool", "[]string", "json.RawMessage", etc.)
      omitempty      : bool — emit `,omitempty` in the json tag
      notes          : str|null — single-line // comment above the field
  ctx.javadoc_summary    : str|null — class-level Go doc comment (// summary above struct)

Type translation hints (Java → Go):
- Java String → Go string
- Java Boolean → Go bool (rarely *bool when nullable)
- Java Integer → Go int (or *int for nullable)
- Java Long → Go int64
- Java Double / BigDecimal → Go float64
- Java List<String> → Go []string
- Java Map<String, X> → Go map[string]X
- Java JsonNode → Go json.RawMessage
- Java nested class → Go nested struct (separate file recommended)

Caller is responsible for resolving Java types to Go types per the
inverse porting guide. The template just emits the resulting Go struct.

ImportOrder is gofmt-enforced — the post-emit `gofmt -s -w` step
canonicalizes whatever this template emits.
#}
package openrtb_ext

{% if ctx.fields | selectattr('go_type', 'equalto', 'json.RawMessage') | list %}
import (
	"encoding/json"
)

{% endif %}
{% if ctx.javadoc_summary %}
// {{ ctx.javadoc_summary }}
{% endif %}
type ExtImp{{ ctx.bidder_class_root }} struct {
{% for field in ctx.fields %}
{% if field.notes %}
	// {{ field.notes }}
{% endif %}
	{{ field.go_name }} {{ field.go_type }} `json:"{{ field.json_tag }}{% if field.omitempty %},omitempty{% endif %}"`
{% endfor %}
}
